BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Brenda Jones :- School Visit (SV). Reviewed options for regulat
 ion strategies to implement at  the  end of  morning  group meeting daily.
  Discussed importance of practicing these regularly when in neutral state 
 so these can be easy to recruit in heightened states. Plan to send handout
 .\n\nRohan Khosh :- School Visit (SV). Set Rohan up in stander. Rohan has 
 grown over summer and is at the  end of range for Dondolino stander. He ca
 nnot  achieve full extension at hips (approx. 160 deg.) or knees (160 deg.
 ). plan to look for medium Easystand in OT/PT inventory. Suggested pausing
  use of stander to Dave (teacher) until I can get a bigger one. Telephone 
 call to mum. Left voicemail  to update her.\n\nEsther Briggs :- School Vis
 it (SV). Conducted Analysis of Sensory Behaviour Inventory with Brenda. Pl
 an to score\, make suggestions.\n\nMandy Turner :-  School Visit (SV). Tri
 aled stylus access to touch screen on Elitebook vs. IdeaPad. Mandy was abl
 e  to activate touchscreen easier with stylus on IdeaPad. IdeaPad activate
 d each target on initial touch whereas Elitebook occasionally required Man
 dy to repeat touch. Mandy also found smaller screen on IdeaPad helpful due
  to her limited range of motion. Plan to write report recommending IdeaPad
 .\n
